>> 1 copy base rootfs
>> 2 bake desktop extensions (setuid preserved under fakeroot)
>> 2c de-brand the baked desktop (wallpaper logo + launcher/menu text)
>> 2d apply the xxri design system over the baked desktop
>> 3 re-apply base setuid bits (chown cleared them)
>> 4 seed desktop config (Xvesa/flwm/wbar tce.installed equivalents)
>> 5 runtime dirs, persistent /tce, writable fstab, dev nodes
>> 6 write ext4 image (label XXRIROOT, 1024M)
>> Done: /home/jantzen/xxri-build/output/xxri-disk.img

Boot it (no root= needed; /init auto-detects LABEL=XXRIROOT):
  qemu-system-x86_64 -enable-kvm -m 1024 \
    -kernel /home/jantzen/xxri-build/work/iso/boot/vmlinuz -initrd /home/jantzen/xxri-build/output/core.gz \
    -append 'loglevel=3' -drive file=/home/jantzen/xxri-build/output/xxri-disk.img,format=raw

Or write it to a real disk/USB (DESTROYS that disk):
  sudo dd if=/home/jantzen/xxri-build/output/xxri-disk.img of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress conv=fsync
